# Python source code

## Import boundaries (CI-enforced)

Three layers: domain → application → infrastructure. Direction is one-way:

- `domain/` must NOT import from `application/` or `infrastructure/`
- `application/` may import from `domain/`, must NOT import from `infrastructure/`
- `infrastructure/` may import from `domain/` and `application/`

Violations fail CI immediately via import-linter. Check locally: `make import-check`

## Verification

Run `make verify` before claiming any task is complete. This runs:
format-check → lint → typecheck → import-check → test-unit → validate-adrs

## Style

- ruff formats and lints (config in pyproject.toml)
- mypy strict mode for type checking
- pytest with 100% coverage threshold on unit tests

## ADRs

Architecture decisions are in `docs/adr/`. Each has a Verification section (command to prove the constraint holds) and a Retirement section (condition under which to remove it). Read the relevant ADR before modifying constrained code.
